und which is  sprawling it's absolutely enormous  within the green zone however as far as  we know so so far they haven't taken any  action  and presumably they will very much be  hoping that they can rely on the Iraqi  security forces to protect the compound  because if the US troops do get involved  that would run the risk of inflaming  things further so are there any steps  then being taken towards some sort of a  resolution or is it just sort of a watch  and see how things develop approach well  we have had a statement from the Iraqi  caretaker Prime Minister this morning  now he condemned the US airstrikes on  Sunday and called the militia fighters  who were killed martyrs but he also  called on the protesters to leave the  embassy alone not to target embassies  within Baghdad however it's not clear  how much impact that will have how  likely it is to deter the protesters  given that there are several quite  powerful political figures within Iraq  that seems to be taking part in these  protests all right Holly thank you so  much for bringing us up to speed
 

